% capacity — the road domains' role vocabulary (road-world s-e812715d step 2), one per vehicle and never per scene, as
% alfworld's capacity.llp: the ego's world in roles the host binds every tick (semantic_world.lane LaneMap.roles and
% zone_roles; metis-worlds road/world/road_facts.py writes the facts). The objects: lead (ahead in the ego's way),
% follower (behind it), leadleft / followleft and leadright / followright (the neighbour lanes'), a1..a3 (the others
% by relevance), vru1 (the walker); the zone: nextzone (the next conflict zone on the ego's route); the sides.
catalog road_capacity 1.
provenance text "the road domains' roles: one capacity per vehicle, bound by the host each tick" "2026-10-26".
type obj {lead follower leadleft followleft leadright followright a1 a2 a3 vru1}.
type side {left right}.
type constel {same_dir opp_dir xing_ego_prio xing_obj_prio xing_same_prio unstructured not_relevant}.
type resp {none brake_min_correct brake_min}.
type before {none long lat both}.
type xcase {able_to_stop safe_long no_overlap none}.
type zone {nextzone}.
type zclass {none far near at in}.
type prio {ego obj same}.
type walk {near on}.
type unst {none continue drive_away brake}.      % the free-space response (situation.RESP_UNST)
type sector {s0 s1 s2 s3 s4 s5 s6 s7}.           % the drive-away heading, quantised (situation.SECTORS)
